all also that there is an augmentation\n<MATH_0021>\nwhere we view <MATH_0022> as a constant simplicial <MATH_0023>-algebra.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e1f30bdd4eeb251e1cbe20429addf0ebdfe53f0c87a01d343af0a01f5cf04312", "unit_id": "tag:08PL:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "08PL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\psi : C \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$A$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0006": "$E \\to B$", "MATH_0007": "$E$", "MATH_0008": "$V : \\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0009": "$U : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0010": "$E \\to B$", "MATH_0011": "$A[E] \\to B$", "MATH_0012": "$X_\\bullet$", "MATH_0013": "$\\text{Fun}(\\mathcal{A}, \\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{A} \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{S} \\ar@<1ex>[l] \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\textit{Alg}_A \\ar[r] & \\textit{Sets} \\ar@<1ex>[l]\n}\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$X_\\bullet(\\text{id}_B : B \\to B)$", "MATH_0016": "$B$", "MATH_0017": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{simplicial-section-standard}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-variant-cotangent-complex}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a9a7bdfbd7b67fca9c893a726461809e341e3d6ff4c1c45f383c5b39d0f8f2ad", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1cdc00791d0fe76c22eb0e80d6907cd0a2772e5a503b4f6b8a3c9613cdf1d12f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ring map. Let <MATH_0002> be the category of\narrows <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004>-algebras and let <MATH_0005> be\nthe category of maps <MATH_0006> where <MATH_0007> is a set. There are adjoint\nfunctors <MATH_0008> (the forgetful functor)\nand <MATH_0009> which sends <MATH_0010> to\n<MATH_0011>. Let <MATH_0012> be the simplicial object of\n<MATH_0013> constructed in\nSimplicial, Section <REF_0001>.\nThe diagram\n<MATH_0014>\ncommutes. It follows that <MATH_0015>\nis equal to the standard resolution of <MATH_0016> over <MATH_0017>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3c6472d3540b884c4a982522738f5321f2976a96b0f4cbf37ac6a9b0601f27a5", "unit_id": "tag:08PP:statement"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08PL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V : A\\textit{-Alg} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$U : \\textit{Sets} \\to A\\textit{-Alg}$", "MATH_0003": "$B/A \\mapsto \\Omega_{B/A}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-colimit-differentials}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8976edba5c9bb8991accac41561347b8e50beba876873a35e104ad84ca8defed", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c542c9a76d808d4b4c97095c3c94dda0ace75b1a1c71971df1677302351713e5", "source_text": "This is true because the forgetful functor\n<MATH_0001> and its adjoint\n<MATH_0002> commute with filtered colimits.\nMoreover, the functor <MATH_0003> does as well\n(Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c8d0a15063b6ae4d3a47235a188348d0789975f9070394702337a83b8f36a7d2", "unit_id": "tag:08S9:proof"}
